    "updated_at": "2017-03-27T12:53:03Z",
    "body": "If I had to guess, some of the browsers may have informally settled on max ascent or something of it's ilk since it's a more useful metric in terms of bounding boxes. If someone wants to position some text by the top left of its bounding box so that all the ascenders are below a certain y coordinate then the top of the em square isn't entirely useful compared to the outer bounding.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if that's what the non-FF browsers are doing, but perhaps that's the motivation, however not per spec.",
