    "updated_at": "2017-06-08T04:55:54Z",
    "body": "> IIUC Gecko uses sTypoAscender and sTypoDescender more than Blink does, so I suspect bottom is where sTypoDescender points to,\r\n\r\nI found this is a long tradition of vertical CJK layout before digital typography, during the period of movable type, Chinese characters usually aligned with descenders especially in books and newspapers printed with vertical layout, in this [file](https://userscloud.com/tqvelmv274wt) you will see the samples.",
