    "created_at": "2017-04-04T08:05:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-04T08:05:25Z",
    "body": "> And does Gecko use sTypoDescender for the bottom of \"em square\"?\r\n\r\nNo, I don't believe so. That could have the effect of putting the top of the em-square unexpectedly low in cases where the font has long descenders. The sTypo* metrics often sum to considerably more than 1em, in which case we would assume that they project both above and below the em-square; we don't stick the em-square to just one edge of the sTypo* bounds.\r\n\r\nWithout going back and reading the code, what I think I recall is that we compute emAscent and emDescent values such that their ratio matches that of sTypoAscender:sTypoDescender, but normalized so that emAscent+emDescent = 1em. These emAscent/emDescent values then determine where \"top\" and \"bottom\" of the em-square occur in relation to the baseline.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
